// Signing.xcconfig — committed stub.
//
// Real signing identity (team ID, bundle ID) lives in Signing.local.xcconfig,
// which is gitignored so personal / org signing details never land in a commit.
//
// To build the iOS target locally, create QuipiOS/Signing.local.xcconfig with:
//     DEVELOPMENT_TEAM = <your 10-char Apple Developer team ID>
//     QUIP_APP_BUNDLE_ID = <your bundle ID, e.g. com.example.quip>
//
// QUIP_APP_BUNDLE_ID, not PRODUCT_BUNDLE_IDENTIFIER: the watch app and the
// Live Activity derive their IDs from it (`<id>.watchkitapp`,
// `<id>.liveactivity`), and the watch's WKCompanionAppBundleIdentifier names
// it. Setting PRODUCT_BUNDLE_IDENTIFIER alone renamed only the phone app, so
// the watch still pointed at com.quip.QuipiOS — it could never pair, and an App
// Store upload rejects a watch app whose ID is not prefixed by its parent's.
// A local file that still sets only PRODUCT_BUNDLE_IDENTIFIER now builds as
// the default below; add QUIP_APP_BUNDLE_ID to it.
//
// The `?` on #include means "include if present" — missing local file is not
// an error here; it will surface at codesign time with a clearer message.

QUIP_APP_BUNDLE_ID = com.quip.QuipiOS
#include? "Signing.local.xcconfig"
